From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: do not let a launch animation swallow the launch

Search results stopped opening. Typing found them and they drew
correctly, but Return did nothing and neither did clicking one.

AppIcon.activate() animates before it activates. The animation zooms a
clone out from the icon's transformed position, and an icon that has not
been allocated answers with a number near the float limit -- about
-3.9e38. That value passes findMonitorForActor and Math.clamp untouched
and is only rejected at the very end, by translation_y, as out of range.
The exception then leaves activate() before app.activate() and before
Main.overview.hide(), so the application never started and the overview
never closed.

Animating from a position that does not exist is not something to
attempt, so it is not attempted; and a launch is not made to depend on
the flourish that accompanies it.

diff --git a/js/ui/iconGrid.js b/js/ui/iconGrid.js
--- a/js/ui/iconGrid.js
+++ b/js/ui/iconGrid.js
@@ -194,6 +194,19 @@
     });
     const [width, height] = actor.get_transformed_size();
 
+    // An actor that has never been allocated has no position to animate from:
+    // get_transformed_position() answers with a number near the float limit,
+    // which survives findMonitorForActor and Math.clamp and only fails at the
+    // end, when translation_y rejects it as out of range. That throw lands in
+    // AppIcon.activate() before the application is activated and before the
+    // overview is hidden, so a search result stopped launching altogether and
+    // the pointer and the Return key both appeared to do nothing at all.
+    // There is nothing to animate from here, so animate nothing.
+    if (![x, y, width, height].every(Number.isFinite)) {
+        actorClone.destroy();
+        return;
+    }
+
     actorClone.set_size(width, height);
     actorClone.set_position(x, y);
     actorClone.opacity = 255;
diff --git a/js/ui/appDisplay.js b/js/ui/appDisplay.js
--- a/js/ui/appDisplay.js
+++ b/js/ui/appDisplay.js
@@ -3068,8 +3068,17 @@
                             this.app.state === Shell.AppState.RUNNING &&
                             (isCtrlPressed || isMiddleButton);
 
-        if (this.app.state === Shell.AppState.STOPPED || openNewWindow)
-            this.animateLaunch();
+        // Launching must not depend on the flourish that accompanies it.
+        // This ran first, so anything it threw took the activation and the
+        // overview with it, and the failure looked like a dead icon rather
+        // than like a broken animation.
+        if (this.app.state === Shell.AppState.STOPPED || openNewWindow) {
+            try {
+                this.animateLaunch();
+            } catch (error) {
+                logError(error, 'Could not animate the launch');
+            }
+        }
 
         if (openNewWindow)
             this.app.open_new_window(-1);
